Z||000000||Elenor84||01-26-2001||02:25 AM||||Well thas over doing it alittle bit but it is pritty bad.  I was in my auto shop class at skool and my teacher told me I probably had a front main leak...can someone explain that to me?  Do u think thats what it is?  I already replaced the valvecover gasket.  But now its leaking from underneithe...anyidea's?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||01-26-2001||02:33 AM||||Is it a 4-cyl or a V-6? V-6 has an O-ring on the distributor that can leak. The 4-cyl has an access panel on the side of the block that is used to access the lifters (it is below the head of the engine). This cover is siliconed on and can leak. Or you could have an oil leak from the oil pan itself. The front and rear main seals could also leak. It is best to clean off the engine then drive the car around a few minutes then go under and see where the oil is coming from.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||01-26-2001||02:38 AM||||2.5 litre....access pannel on the side?  Witch side would it be on exactly?  I will do just that and clean her off and driver her and look...thx for the tips!<P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||1
Z||000003||Elenor84||01-26-2001||02:38 AM||||2.5 litre....access pannel on the side?  Witch side would it be on exactly?  I will do just that and clean her off and driver her and look...thx for the tips!<P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||1
